# Known-fake examples that tools/leakcheck may ignore. Each line is a regex
# matched against the flagged text (an email address, a path, an IP).
# Only generic matches can be allowed - never private patterns.
#
# Prefer example.com for anything new. These are the fakes already in the
# docs and in tools/screenshot.py, which draws rack.svg.
^you@
^claude-[0-9]+@work\.com$
^you\.example@gmail\.com$
